The `retrieveAndProcessPokemonData` method takes a query parameter as input and makes multiple requests to the external API in parallel using an `ExecutorService`. Each request is executed with a retry logic that includes exponential backoff, which helps mitigate cascading failures. The service also monitors the health of the external APIs and dynamically adjusts data fetching strategies based on their availability.

The `makeRequest` method handles API requests to the external service using an HTTP client. It implements retry logic with configurable backoff strategies, which helps handle transient errors. The method also includes error handling mechanisms to gracefully handle API errors and incomplete data responses.

