1. Lexer and Parser
-------------------

To implement a flexible lexer and parser, we will use the `nom` crate for Rust's lexing and parsing functionality. The `nom` crate provides an easy-to-use API for defining grammars and implementing parsing algorithms. We will define multiple grammars in separate modules, each representing a different grammar. We will also implement incremental parsing for streaming inputs, allowing the AST to be updated in real-time as new data arrives.
```rust
use nom::{Parser};

struct Lexer {
    // ...
}

impl Parser<String> for Lexer {
    fn parse(input: &str) -> Result<String, String> {
        // Parse the input string using the lexer.
        let mut parser = Lexer::new();
        match parser.parse_all(input) {
            Ok((remaining_input, tokens)) => {
                // Return the parsed tokens as a list of strings.
                return Ok((remaining_input, tokens));
            },
            Err(e) => {
                return Err(format!("Error parsing input: {}", e));
            }
        }
    }
}
```
