### 3.2 Implementation of the classes

The `Aggregator` class is responsible for collecting events from various sources and aggregating them into a single stream. It does this by maintaining a list of event sources and delegating the collection of events to each source. When a new event is added to the aggregator, it is passed to all the registered event sources.

The `EventSource` class represents an external source of events that can be aggregated. The `getEvents()` method returns the latest events from the source.

The `Sensor` class represents a single sensor in the system. It has a unique ID and maintains its own value. The `getValue()` method retrieves the current value of the sensor from an external source.

