The implementation uses the `Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration` package to load configuration values from an external source, such as a JSON file or environment variables. It also uses the `Newtonsoft.Json` package for JSON serialization and deserialization.

The library supports both MD5 and SHA-256 hash algorithms, and it can be configured to use either one by specifying the desired algorithm in the configuration file. If an invalid or unsupported algorithm is specified, the method will throw a `NotSupportedException`.

