The `Library` class is the main entry point of the library, and it provides functions for hashing and storing input data. The `HashAndStoreAsync` function takes a string input, computes its hash using an instance of `IHashAlgorithm`, and stores it in the specified data store using an instance of `IDataStore`. The `GetStoredInputAsync` function retrieves the original input string from the specified data store using an instance of `IDataStore` based on the provided hash.

The library uses dependency injection to inject instances of `ILogger`, `IConfiguration`, and `IServiceProvider` into its functions. It also utilizes a service provider to create instances of third-party services such as threat intelligence and data store services.

The library is designed to be highly configurable, with support for multiple data stores and third-party APIs. The user can specify the type of data store to use in the configuration file, and the library will automatically instantiate an instance of `IDataStore` based on the specified data store type. Similarly, the user can specify the types of threat intelligence and machine learning models to use, and the library will automatically instantiate instances of `IThreatIntelligenceService` and `IMachineLearningService`.

The library also utilizes intelligent caching strategies to optimize performance and cost-efficiency. It uses a combination of in-memory caching and disk-based caching to store frequently accessed data, and it provides mechanisms for manual cache invalidation and optimization. The user can configure the cache settings using the configuration file, and the library will automatically adjust its cache settings based on the current workload and historical patterns.

The library is designed to be highly secure, with support for encryption at rest and in transit, multi-factor authentication, and advanced security features such as threat intelligence and machine learning. The user can configure the security settings using the configuration file, and the library will automatically apply these settings based on the specified data store type and third-party APIs used.

