};
```
8. Resource Management and Scalability
--------------------------------------

To efficiently manage system resources and ensure scalability under high load, we can use asynchronous processing and an event-driven architecture to handle concurrent operations and reduce contention. We will also implement resource monitoring and auto-scaling mechanisms to adapt to varying workloads.
```c++
class ResourceManager {
public:
    void manage(); // Manage system resources (e.g., CPU, memory)
private:
    std::unordered_map<std::string, double> _resourceUsage; // Map of resource usage statistics
};
```
9. Trade-offs and Implementation Decisions
-------------------------------------------

To make informed trade-offs between performance, usability, and maintainability, we will consider the implications of different architectural decisions on system reliability, latency, and development complexity. We will also perform thorough testing and benchmarking to ensure that the library meets its performance, scalability, and reliability goals under different network conditions and message types.
```c++
class Implementation {
public:
