To handle unpredictable transaction volumes, intermittent API service disruptions, and variable network conditions, this code uses a retry logic with exponential backoff and a circuit breaker pattern. The retry attempts are defined by the `retryAttempts` member variable, which can be adjusted as needed. The exponential backoff factor is defined by the `exponentialBackoffFactor` member variable, which controls how long to wait between retries. If the circuit breaker is enabled, it will timeout after a certain period of time has passed without receiving any responses from the payment gateway.

To balance performance optimizations with the complexity of the system and maintenance overhead, this code leverages profile-guided optimizations (PGO) and tiered caching strategies to reduce latency and improve throughput. PGO can help identify frequently executed parts of the code and optimize them for better performance. Tiered caching strategies can be used to store frequently accessed data in memory or on disk, depending on their size and access patterns.

To support mobile applications and web interfaces, this code provides SDKs and APIs for seamless integration with third-party developers. It also implements a multi-tenant architecture to support shared hosting environments, which allows multiple tenants to share the same instance of the payment gateway without affecting each other.

