4. We also need to define a function that takes a directory path and renames all of the files in it based on their categories. This function can use the `renameFile` function to rename each file individually.
```c++
void renameFilesInDirectory(const std::string& directoryPath) {
    // Get the list of files in the directory
    auto files = getFilesInDirectory(directoryPath);

    // Rename each file in the directory based on its category
    for (auto& file : files) {
        renameFile(file.path());
    }
}
```
