In terms of implementing the union-find data structure for efficiently checking disjointness between log entries, we will use a combination of a hash map and a linked list. The hash map will be used to store the union find tree structure, while the linked list will be used to store the nodes that are part of the union find tree.

Here is an example Java function that takes an integer array as input and returns the number of disjoint pairs of elements in the array:
```java
public int countDisjointPairs(int[] arr) {
  // Create a hash map to store the union find tree structure
  Map<Integer, Node> nodes = new HashMap<>();

  // Initialize the linked list for storing nodes that are part of the union find tree
  List<Node> nodeList = new LinkedList<>();

  // Iterate over the array and check if each element is disjoint from all other elements
  int count = 0;
  for (int i = 0; i < arr.length - 1; i++) {
    Node n1 = nodes.get(arr[i]);
    if (n1 == null) {
      // If the element is not part of the union find tree, create a new node and add it to the linked list
      Node newNode = new Node(arr[i], i);
      nodes.put(newNode.value, newNode);
      nodeList.addLast(newNode);
    } else {
      // If the element is already part of the union find tree, check if it is disjoint from all other elements
      for (int j = i + 1; j < arr.length; j++) {
        Node n2 = nodes.get(arr[j]);
        if (n2 == null) {
          // If the element is not part of the union find tree, create a new node and add it to the linked list
          Node newNode = new Node(arr[j], j);
          nodes.put(newNode.value, newNode);
          nodeList.addLast(newNode);
        } else {
          // If the element is already part of the union find tree, check if it is disjoint from all other elements
          boolean disjoint = true;
          for (int k = 0; k < j; k++) {
            if (nodes.get(arr[k]).unionFindRoot == nodes.get(arr[j]).unionFindRoot) {
              // If the element is not disjoint from any other element, set disjoint to false and break out of the loop
              disjoint = false;
              break;
            }
          }
          if (disjoint) {
            count++;
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
  return count;
}
```
This function uses a combination of a hash map and a linked list to store the union find tree structure and the nodes that are part of the union find tree. It then iterates over the input array and checks if each element is disjoint from all other elements using a nested loop. If an element is not part of the union find tree, it creates a new node and adds it to the linked list. If an element is already part of the union find tree, it checks if it is disjoint from all other elements by iterating over all elements that are part of the same union find tree as the current element. If an element is not disjoint with any other element, it sets a boolean variable to false and breaks out of the loop. Finally, it returns the number of disjoint pairs of elements in the array."]

