This is the output I get when I run ```pip show networkx```. The version number seems to be 2.5, but I am not sure if that means the latest version or not. If it is not the latest version, how can I update it?

Comment: If you are using a virtual environment, do `pip install --upgrade networkx` (this assumes you have already done `pip install networkx`) to upgrade the library to its latest version. Else, do `pip install --upgrade pip` and then try again.

Answer: \begin{blockquote}
The version number seems to be 2.5, but I am not sure if that means the latest version or not. If it is not the latest version, how can I update it?
\end{blockquote}

You can check [this](https://pypi.org/project/networkx/) and see if there is a newer version available for NetworkX. You should be able to check this by running `pip search networkx` and then looking at the version number in the results. If it's outdated, you can try updating it with `pip install --upgrade networkx`.

Answer: The latest stable release of NetworkX is 2.6rc1, which was released on 2021-08-04. So you may need to run

\begin{code}
pip install -U networkx==2.6rc1
\end{code}"]

