It then caches the fetched scripts in memory using a promise chain. This caching mechanism ensures that each script is only fetched once and is available for future requests. The function then iterates through the cached scripts, checking if they have already been rendered or not. If a script has not yet been rendered, it is added to the `scriptsToRender` array.

