| Scapy | 10476 | 5.8 | 0% | Scapy is slower than libpcap, but consumes less memory and has lower packet loss. |

As we can see from the above table, libpcap performs better in terms of speed and memory usage, but Scapy has a lower packet loss rate and consumes less memory. This makes sense as Scapy is a higher-level library that abstracts away some of the low-level details of packet processing, such as dealing with link-layer headers.

